From: WLAN Pi <wlanpi-kernel local patch>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: advertise MLD/EML capabilities on the station iftype

ath12k_mac_hw_register() copies the firmware's MLO capabilities
(WMI_SERVICE_READY_EXT2 eml_cap / mld_cap) into ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[2],
which is the NL80211_IFTYPE_AP entry. The array is laid out as:

  [0] default (no iftype)
  [1] NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION
  [2] NL80211_IFTYPE_AP

mac80211 builds the Basic Multi-Link element of a station's
(Re)Association Request from the STATION entry, which is left at zero.
A WCN7850 client therefore advertises MLD Capabilities 0x0000
(Maximum Number of Simultaneous Links = 0, one link at a time) and no
EML Capabilities, even though the firmware reports
single_chip_mlo_support = 1. The AP then keeps all traffic on a single
link.

Write the capabilities to the STATION entry instead, and cap one field
of the firmware's mld_cap (0x0042 on WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108): Maximum
Number of Simultaneous Links is encoded as the link count minus one.
The firmware's 2 claims three links, but QMI reports num_link 2. Cap it
at 1 (two simultaneous links).

TID-To-Link Mapping Negotiation Support is passed through as the
firmware reports it (2). ath12k does not implement can_neg_ttlm, so
mac80211 still rejects any negotiation request.

The resulting station capabilities are MLD 0x0041 and EML 0x2037
(EMLSR supported, no EMLMR). The client can use both links at once,
and ath12k passes the AP's EMLSR capability to firmware in the peer
assoc ML params, so firmware can fall back to EMLSR when the AP
supports it.

The WLAN Pi only runs ath12k as a client, so AP-mode MLD advertisement
is not needed here.

Observed on wlanpi-511 (WCN7850 hw2.0, fw WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108) with
wlanpi-kernel 7.2.6 and 7.2.7: the Reassociation Request carries
MLD Capabilities 0x0000 and no EML field, while the AP response
advertises EMLSR and Max Simultaneous Links = 2 (three links).

Local WLAN Pi patch (not from ath-next). Re-check on every kernel bump:
drop it once upstream writes the station entry.

---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -14938,8 +14938,17 @@
 	 * WMI_SERVICE_READY_EXT2_EVENT if single_chip_mlo_supp is set.
 	 */
 	if (ab->ag->mlo_capable) {
-		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[2].eml_capabilities = cap->eml_cap;
-		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[2].mld_capa_and_ops = cap->mld_cap;
+		u16 mld_cap = cap->mld_cap;
+
+		/* The field is the link count minus one. Firmware reports 2
+		 * (three links) but QMI reports num_link 2, so cap it at 1.
+		 */
+		if (u16_get_bits(mld_cap, IEEE80211_MLD_CAP_OP_MAX_SIMUL_LINKS) > 1)
+			u16p_replace_bits(&mld_cap, 1,
+					  IEEE80211_MLD_CAP_OP_MAX_SIMUL_LINKS);
+
+		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[1].eml_capabilities = cap->eml_cap;
+		ath12k_iftypes_ext_capa[1].mld_capa_and_ops = mld_cap;
 		wiphy->flags |= WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_MLO;
 
 		ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MLO_MCAST_MULTI_LINK_TX);
